      },
      "text": "By the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the \nlaws of the United States of America and pursuant to the Federal Vacancies \nReform Act of 1998, 5 U.S.C. 3345 et seq., it is hereby ordered that:"
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2134,
      "char_start": 940,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:13370#sec1",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Section 1.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:13370#sec1",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "70 FR 3137, PDF pages 1-2",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "f8a7bc905ec783521ad95f158087eff95ff08d17f0276ed94e4850618741af04",
        "signing_date": "2005-01-13",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_13370.txt",
        "text_sha256": "a75e9e261987a9b6e2d60c06fe2cea2ae88fe103b82edfab76de44d62018c631",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-19/pdf/05-1170.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Section 1. During any period when the Director of the Office of Management \nand Budget (Director) and the Deputy Director of the Office of Management \nand Budget (Deputy Director) have died, resigned, or otherwise become \nunable to perform the functions and duties of the office of Director, the \nfollowing officers of the Office of Management and Budget, in the order \nlisted, shall perform the functions and duties of the office of Director, \nif they are eligible to act as Director under the provisions of the Federal \nVacancies Reform Act of 1998, until such time as at least one of the officers \nmentioned above is able to perform the functions and duties of the office \nof Director: \nDeputy Director for Management; \nExecutive Associate Director; \nAssociate Director (National Security Programs); \nAssociate Director (General Government Programs); \nAssociate Director (Human Resource Programs); \nAssociate Director (Natural Resource Programs); \nGeneral Counsel; \nAdministrator for Federal Procurement Policy; \nAdministrator of the Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs; \nController, Office of Federal Financial Management; and \nAdministrator of the Office of Electronic Government."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2552,
      "char_start": 2136,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:13370#sec2",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Sec. 2.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:13370#sec2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "70 FR 3137, PDF pages 1-2",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "f8a7bc905ec783521ad95f158087eff95ff08d17f0276ed94e4850618741af04",
        "signing_date": "2005-01-13",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_13370.txt",
        "text_sha256": "a75e9e261987a9b6e2d60c06fe2cea2ae88fe103b82edfab76de44d62018c631",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-19/pdf/05-1170.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Sec. 2. Exceptions. (a) No individual who is serving in an office listed \nin section 1 in an acting capacity, by virtue of so serving, shall act as \nDirector pursuant to this order. \nVerDate jul<14>2003 15:21 Jan 18, 2005 Jkt 205001 PO 00000 Frm 00003 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\19JAE0.SGM 19JAE0\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n3138 Federal Register / Vol. 70, No. 12 / Wednesday, January 19, 2005 / Presidential Documents"
    },
